        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Boorman, Patricia Arquette, Victor Slezak, Laura Bowman\n- Films: Beyond Rangoon, True Romance, Ed Wood, Flirting with Disaster, Lost Highway, The Hi-Lo Country, Bringing Out the Dead, Holes, The Bridges of Madison County, The Devil's Own, The Siege, The Cat's Meow, Timequest, The Notorious Bettie Page\n- Places: Burma, Myanmar\n- Events: 8888 Uprising\n\nFacts:\n- In 1988, the 8888 Uprising took place in Burma, also known as Myanmar.\n- Beyond Rangoon is a 1995 drama film directed by John Boorman.\n- Beyond Rangoon is about Laura Bowman, an American tourist played by Patricia Arquette, who vacations in Burma in 1988 during the 8888 Uprising.\n- Victor Slezak, born on July 30, 1957, is an American stage, television, and screen actor.\n- Patricia Arquette's notable films include True Romance (1993), Ed Wood (1994), Flirting with Disaster (1996), Lost Highway (1997), The Hi-Lo Country (1998), Bringing Out the Dead (1999), and Holes (2003).\n- Victor Slezak appeared in The Bridges of Madison County (1995), Beyond Rangoon (1995), The Devil's Own (1997), The Siege (1998), The Cat's Meow (2001), Timequest as John F. Kennedy (2002), and The Notorious Bettie Page (2005).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
